* in-suite TEST R^2 = comparable to run_probe.py's IN-SUITE R^2 (same sim_split seed 0).
* xR2    = cross-suite, held-out standardized by TRAIN(in-suite) stats ('as-deployed').
* xR2sn  = cross-suite, held-out SELF-normalized by its own stats (removes per-suite
           offset) = fair analog of the SSL probe self-normalizing SIMBA inputs.
  Read: xR2 << xR2sn -> the collapse was amplitude-EXTRAPOLATION; xR2sn still low ->
        genuine SHAPE-transfer failure. Compare xR2sn to the SSL probe's held-out R^2.
